<GuideLayout 
  title="The Logistics of Scale: Why DDP Shipping is a Game Changer for B2B Buyers" 
  type="STRATEGY"
  description="How DDP terms can simplify activewear imports when the destination and logistics route support them. Request a route-specific quote."
>
  <h2>Worry-Free Importing: The DDP Advantage</h2>
  <p>Customs, import duties and local clearance can complicate landed-cost planning. <strong>DDP (Delivered Duty Paid)</strong> may simplify an order when a suitable route is available and its scope is confirmed in writing.</p>
  
  <h3>What is DDP?</h3>
  <p>Under an agreed DDP sale, the seller arranges delivery to the named destination and takes on the duties specified by the agreed Incoterm. The quote must identify the named place, covered charges and any exclusions. {businessFacts.shipping}</p>

  <h3>When to Consider DDP</h3>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-4 my-6 text-gray-700">
    <li><strong>Comparable quotes:</strong> Ask which freight, duty, tax and local charges are included for the named destination.</li>
    <li><strong>Clear responsibilities:</strong> Confirm importer requirements and documents for the specific country and route.</li>
    <li><strong>Delivery planning:</strong> Review the estimated transit separately from sample development, production and dispatch.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="mt-12 p-8 bg-[#C9A84C]/5 border border-[#C9A84C]/20 rounded-2xl">
    <h4 class="text-[#C9A84C] font-bold mb-4">Request a DDP Quote</h4>
    <p class="text-gray-500 mb-6">Share the destination address, style, quantity and expected packed weight. We can check whether DDP is available on the actual route and quote its scope, cost and estimated transit.</p>
    <a href="/#inquiry" class="inline-block bg-[#C9A84C] text-black px-8 py-3 rounded-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wider transition-all hover:bg-[#b8973d]">Get Shipping Quote →</a>
  </div>
</GuideLayout>
